cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Mjolnir: resistance, lineage, species and contamination calling for the Mycobacterium tuberculosis complex and non-tuberculous mycobacteria"
message: "If you use Mjolnir, please cite it and the catalogues and reference databases it called from - 'mjolnir db list' prints each one's version, licence and citation, and every report Mjolnir writes carries the same list."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "Mjolnir contributors"
    affiliation: ""
repository-code: "https://github.com/iowa69/mjolnir"
url: "https://github.com/iowa69/mjolnir"
abstract: >-
  Mjolnir calls species, lineage, drug resistance and contamination for the
  Mycobacterium tuberculosis complex and for non-tuberculous mycobacteria, from
  Illumina reads, ONT reads or assemblies, in one command and one report.
  Resistance is called independently from the WHO catalogue of mutations
  (2nd edition), MTBseq's resistance-mediating lists and tbdb, then reconciled
  with WHO as the anchor; a variant WHO does not grade but another catalogue
  calls resistant is reported as resistant outside the WHO catalogue rather than
  dropped or promoted. Species identification is ANI-based rather than taxonomic
  read classification, because MTBC members are not at species rank in NCBI
  taxonomy; lineage comes from SNP barcodes read off a direct pileup and is
  reported with its barcode support, since BCG and the animal lineages rest on
  as few as five defining SNPs. Contamination is reported as a sample-validity
  verdict from the signals that can honestly be measured in mycobacteria.
  Absence of a resistance determinant is reported as absence, never as
  susceptibility, and every threshold in the tool carries the document it came
  from.
keywords:
  - tuberculosis
  - mycobacteria
  - nontuberculous mycobacteria
  - antimicrobial resistance
  - lineage typing
  - contamination
  - outbreak investigation
  - genomics
license: MIT
